# Organic Logic: A Generative Framework for Living Systems

## Classic Logic, Anti-Logic, and the Middle Way of Homogenesis

---

**Abstract:** This article presents the development of Organic Logic—a generative framework that synthesizes Classic Logic (true/false binary) and Anti-Logic (opposition/negation) into a living, dynamic system. Organic Logic recognizes that true and false are approachable ideals, that the middle is *homogenesis*—the generative ground from which opposition emerges—and that contradictions are natural features of organic systems. Using GFF-1 as the foundational meta-framework, we demonstrate that Organic Logic is not a rejection of classical logic but an *expansion* of it—one that acknowledges loss, embraces dynamics, and honors the living complexity of reality.

